 2017"},"354":{"id":"/features/atomics-51","page_id":"/features/atomics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/atomics#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2017-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"355":{"id":"/features/bigint","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"page","content":"BigInt","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2020"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint"},"356":{"id":"/features/bigint-0","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#bigint","content":"BigInt"},"357":{"id":"/features/bigint-1","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"358":{"id":"/features/bigint-2","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"359":{"id":"/features/bigint-3","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"360":{"id":"/features/bigint-4","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#support","content":"Support"},"361":{"id":"/features/bigint-5","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#related","content":"Related"},"362":{"id":"/features/bigint-6","page_id":"/features/bigint","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"363":{"id":"/features/bigint-7","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#bigint","content":"BigInt adds a second numeric primitive whose integers carry arbitrary precision and refuse to mix with `Number` in arithmetic."},"364":{"id":"/features/bigint-8","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#what-it-does","content":"`NumericLiteral` gains a `BigIntLiteralSuffix`, the character `n`, on a decimal literal without a fractional part or exponent and on binary, octal, and hexadecimal literals. `BigInt(value)` converts instead of constructing: it throws a `TypeError` when called with `new`, and routes a `Number` argument through `NumberToBigInt`, which rejects a non-integer with a `RangeError`. Each arithmetic operator applies `ToNumeric` to both operands and throws a `TypeError` when the two results have different types, then dispatches to the operation of the shared type, so `/` on two BigInts truncates toward zero. Loose equality across the two types compares mathematical values, and any `NaN` or infinite operand makes the comparison false. `BigInt.asUintN(bits, bigint)` reduces its argument modulo 2 to the power of `bits`, which is how a fixed-width value is produced. The proposal's stated reason for refusing mixed arithmetic is that no implicit conversion between the two types is safe."},"365":{"id":"/features/bigint-9","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#gotchas","content":"`+` is the one arithmetic operator that accepts a mixed pair, and only with a string: `1n + \"2\"` produces `\"12\"` while `1n + 1` throws. Unary `+` is rejected on a BigInt, because it reaches `ToNumber`, whose BigInt row throws a `TypeError`; the same row is why every `Math` method rejects one. Serialization fails rather than degrading: `SerializeJSONProperty` throws a `TypeError` for a BigInt value, so a payload holding one needs a `toJSON` method or a replacer, and that clause does consult `toJSON` on a BigInt. Converting a large `Number` literal loses digits before `BigInt` ever sees them, so `BigInt(9007199254740993)` yields `9007199254740992n` while the string form `BigInt(\"9007199254740993\")` is exact. `0n` is falsy, so a guard written as `if (count)` treats an explicit zero the same way it treats a missing value."},"366":{"id":"/features/bigint-10","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#support","content":"V8 shipped the type in 6.7 with the feature enabled by default, described there as a numeric primitive for integers of arbitrary precision."},"367":{"id":"/features/bigint-11","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#related","content":"exponentiation-operator"},"368":{"id":"/features/bigint-12","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"BigInt: Arbitrary precision integers in JavaScript § interoperation-with-number-and-string"},"369":{"id":"/features/bigint-13","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"370":{"id":"/features/bigint-14","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Numeric Literals"},"371":{"id":"/features/bigint-15","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"372":{"id":"/features/bigint-16","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: BigInt ( value )"},"373":{"id":"/features/bigint-17","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"374":{"id":"/features/bigint-18","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Multiplicative Operators, Runtime Semantics: Evaluation"},"375":{"id":"/features/bigint-19","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"376":{"id":"/features/bigint-20","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: ToNumber ( argument )"},"377":{"id":"/features/bigint-21","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"378":{"id":"/features/bigint-22","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Abstract Equality Comparison"},"379":{"id":"/features/bigint-23","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"380":{"id":"/features/bigint-24","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: BigInt.asUintN ( bits, bigint )"},"381":{"id":"/features/bigint-25","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"382":{"id":"/features/bigint-26","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: SerializeJSONProperty"},"383":{"id":"/features/bigint-27","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"384":{"id":"/features/bigint-28","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"TC39 notes: BigInt to Stage 4"},"385":{"id":"/features/bigint-29","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2019-06-04, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"386":{"id":"/features/bigint-30","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"V8 release v6.7: JavaScript language features"},"387":{"id":"/features/bigint-31","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"Engine record, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"388":{"id":"/features/bigint-32","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 119th General Assembly"},"389":{"id":"/features/bigint-33","page_id":"/features/bigint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/bigint#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"390":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"page","content":"Change Array by copy","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2023"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy"},"391":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-0","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#change-array-by-copy","content":"Change Array by copy"},"392":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-1","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"393":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-2","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"394":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-3","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"395":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-4","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"396":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-5","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#change-array-by-copy","content":"Four array methods reorder, splice, and replace elements by returning a new array, leaving the receiver unchanged."},"397":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-6","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#what-it-does","content":"`toReversed()`, `toSorted(comparefn)`, `toSpliced(start, skipCount, ...items)`, and `with(index, value)` allocate a result array of the required length and fill it from the receiver, which stays untouched. `toReversed` builds that array by reading each source index in reverse. Typed arrays receive `toReversed`, `toSorted`, and `with`, which the proposal lists without `toSpliced`; its champion reported at the Stage 4 request that typed arrays had dropped `toSpliced` during Stage 3. Its stated motivation is code that treats arrays and immutable sequences interchangeably."},"398":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-7","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#gotchas","content":"`with` throws a `RangeError` once the resolved index reaches the length or stays below zero, so it cannot append the way `array[array.length] = value` does. The copies are dense: `[\"p\", , \"r\"].toReversed()` has an own property at every index because each source index is read and stored. Sorting defaults differ by receiver, since the typed-array closure compares numerically instead of using the string comparison of `Array.prototype.toSorted`: `[10, 9, 1].toSorted()` yields `[1, 10, 9]` while `new Uint8Array([10, 9, 1]).toSorted()` yields `[1, 9, 10]`. `Array.prototype.toSorted` also rejects a non-callable comparator with a `TypeError` before touching the receiver."},"399":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-8","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Change Array by copy proposal § overview"},"400":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-9","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"401":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-10","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Change Array by copy proposal § motivation"},"402":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-11","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"403":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-12","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2023: Array.prototype.toReversed"},"404":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-13","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"405":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-14","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2023: Array.prototype.toSorted"},"406":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-15","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"407":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-16","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2023: Array.prototype.toSpliced"},"408":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-17","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"409":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-18","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2023: Array.prototype.with"},"410":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-19","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"411":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-20","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2023: %TypedArray%.prototype.toSorted"},"412":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-21","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"413":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-22","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Change Array by Copy for Stage 4"},"414":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-23","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2023-01-30, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"415":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-24","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"TC39 notes: change-array-by-copy for Stage 3"},"416":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-25","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2022-03-30, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"417":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-26","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 125th General Assembly"},"418":{"id":"/features/change-array-by-copy-27","page_id":"/features/change-array-by-copy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/change-array-by-copy#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2023-06-27, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"419":{"id":"/features/class-fields","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"page","content":"Class field declarations","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2022"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields"},"420":{"id":"/features/class-fields-0","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#class-field-declarations","content":"Class field declarations"},"421":{"id":"/features/class-fields-1","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"422":{"id":"/features/class-fields-2","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"423":{"id":"/features/class-fields-3","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"424":{"id":"/features/class-fields-4","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#related","content":"Related"},"425":{"id":"/features/class-fields-5","page_id":"/features/class-fields","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"426":{"id":"/features/class-fields-6","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#class-field-declarations","content":"A class body declares instance state directly, and a leading `#` restricts a declared name to code written inside that body."},"427":{"id":"/features/class-fields-7","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#what-it-does","content":"A class body accepts a `FieldDefinition`, which is a `ClassElementName` with an optional initializer, and a `ClassElementName` may be a `PrivateIdentifier` written with a leading `#`. A public field is installed with `CreateDataPropertyOrThrow`, and a declaration with no initializer installs the value `undefined`. A private field is appended to the instance's `[[PrivateElements]]` list instead of becoming a property, and a second attempt to add the same private name to one object throws a `TypeError`. Reading a private name from an object that carries no matching entry also throws a `TypeError`. Field declarations, private methods, and static class features were requested in one agenda item, and the committee advanced all three in a single decision. The proposal's stated aim is that declared state is visible in the class definition and present on every instance."},"428":{"id":"/features/class-fields-8","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#gotchas","content":"Because `DefineField` calls `CreateDataPropertyOrThrow`, a subclass declaration of `x = 1` over a base-class `set x(value)` produces an own writable, enumerable, configurable data property and never runs that setter; the proposal names this the `[[Define]]` decision and points at the decorators proposal for opting back into assignment. A bare `y;` in a subclass is not a no-op: it installs `undefined` and hides the value an inherited `y = 1` declaration produced. Private state cannot be introduced after the fact, since the proposal offers private fields only through an up-front declaration, so `object.#step = 1` on a foreign object throws instead of creating an entry."},"429":{"id":"/features/class-fields-9","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#related","content":"private-methods-and-accessors"},"430":{"id":"/features/class-fields-10","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#related","content":"static-class-features"},"431":{"id":"/features/class-fields-11","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#related","content":"class-static-block"},"432":{"id":"/features/class-fields-12","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#related","content":"ergonomic-brand-checks"},"433":{"id":"/features/class-fields-13","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Class field declarations for JavaScript proposal § field-declarations"},"434":{"id":"/features/class-fields-14","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"435":{"id":"/features/class-fields-15","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Class field declarations for JavaScript proposal § public-fields-created-with-objectdefineproperty"},"436":{"id":"/features/class-fields-16","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"437":{"id":"/features/class-fields-17","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Class field declarations for JavaScript proposal § private-fields"},"438":{"id":"/features/class-fields-18","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"439":{"id":"/features/class-fields-19","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: Class Definitions grammar"},"440":{"id":"/features/class-fields-20","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"441":{"id":"/features/class-fields-21","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: DefineField"},"442":{"id":"/features/class-fields-22","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"443":{"id":"/features/class-fields-23","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: PrivateFieldAdd"},"444":{"id":"/features/class-fields-24","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"445":{"id":"/features/class-fields-25","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: PrivateGet"},"446":{"id":"/features/class-fields-26","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"447":{"id":"/features/class-fields-27","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Class fields, Private methods, and Static class features for Stage 4"},"448":{"id":"/features/class-fields-28","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2021-04-19, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"449":{"id":"/features/class-fields-29","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 123rd General Assembly"},"450":{"id":"/features/class-fields-30","page_id":"/features/class-fields","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-fields#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"451":{"id":"/features/class-static-block","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"page","content":"Class static initialization blocks","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2022"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block"},"452":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-0","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#class-static-initialization-blocks","content":"Class static initialization blocks"},"453":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-1","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"454":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-2","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"455":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-3","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"456":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-4","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#related","content":"Related"},"457":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-5","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"458":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-6","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#class-static-initialization-blocks","content":"A `static { … }` member runs statements once during class definition, with the constructor as `this` and access to the class's private names."},"459":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-7","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#what-it-does","content":"`ClassElement` gains a `ClassStaticBlock` production, `static { ClassStaticBlockStatementList }`. Its body becomes a zero-parameter function created in the surrounding lexical and private environments, with the class as its home object. Class definition evaluation puts static blocks and static fields into one `staticElements` list and processes them in source order, calling the block's body function with the constructor as its `this` value. The proposal targets initialization that a single field initializer cannot express, such as a `try`/`catch` or setting two static fields from one computed value, and sharing a private name with a function declared in the same scope."},"460":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-8","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#gotchas","content":"A block is not an async function and not a method body. Its early errors reject a body that contains `await` or `arguments`, and the statement list is parsed with the `Return` parameter absent, so `await fetch(url)`, `arguments`, and a bare `return` inside `static { … }` are all parse failures rather than run-time errors. Ordering is positional, not grouped: since static fields and blocks share one ordered list, a block placed above `static c = …` observes `c` as `undefined`, while one placed below it reads the assigned value. A class may hold several blocks, and each runs at its own position."},"461":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-9","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#related","content":"class-fields"},"462":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-10","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#related","content":"static-class-features"},"463":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-11","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMAScript class static initialization blocks proposal § motivations"},"464":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-12","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"465":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-13","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: Class Definitions grammar"},"466":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-14","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"467":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-15","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: ClassStaticBlockDefinitionEvaluation"},"468":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-16","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"469":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-17","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: ClassDefinitionEvaluation"},"470":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-18","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"471":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-19","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: Class Definitions early errors"},"472":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-20","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"473":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-21","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Class static initialization blocks for Stage 4"},"474":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-22","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2021-08-31, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"475":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-23","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 123rd General Assembly"},"476":{"id":"/features/class-static-block-24","page_id":"/features/class-static-block","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/class-static-block#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"477":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"page","content":"Deferring Module Evaluation","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ESNext"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation"},"478":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-0","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#deferring-module-evaluation","content":"Deferring Module Evaluation"},"479":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-1","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"480":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-2","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"481":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-3","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"482":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-4","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"483":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-5","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#deferring-module-evaluation","content":"`import defer` loads and links a module graph while postponing synchronous evaluation until namespace access."},"484":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-6","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#what-it-does","content":"`import defer * as namespace from \"./module.js\"` produces a module namespace exotic object. Reading one of its properties synchronously triggers evaluation if the module has not run. Loading still prepares the complete dependency graph and populates the module cache. The proposed semantics separate loading from evaluation."},"485":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-7","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#gotchas","content":"The binding must be a namespace binding. Modules with top-level `await`, plus the asynchronous portion of their transitive graph, are evaluated eagerly because namespace property access cannot pause for asynchronous evaluation."},"486":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-8","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"TC39 active proposals at the cutoff"},"487":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-9","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"TC39 stage record, published 2026-07-22, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"488":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-10","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"Deferring Module Evaluation § proposal"},"489":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-11","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"490":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-12","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"Deferring Module Evaluation § semantics"},"491":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-13","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"492":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-14","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"Deferring Module Evaluation § top-level-await"},"493":{"id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation-15","page_id":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/deferred-module-evaluation#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"494":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"page","content":"Duplicate named capture groups","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2025"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups"},"495":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-0","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#duplicate-named-capture-groups","content":"Duplicate named capture groups"},"496":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-1","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"497":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-2","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"498":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-3","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"499":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-4","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#related","content":"Related"},"500":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-5","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"501":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-6","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#duplicate-named-capture-groups","content":"Disjoint alternatives in a regular expression can reuse one capture-group name."},"502":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-7","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#what-it-does","content":"At most one group with the duplicated name can participate in a match. The match result's `groups` property and a named backreference use the participating capture."},"503":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-8","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#gotchas","content":"Reusing a name where both groups can participate remains a syntax error. A named backreference whose group occurs only in another alternative matches the empty string, following existing unmatched-backreference behavior."},"504":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-9","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#related","content":"regexp-modifiers"},"505":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-10","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#related","content":"regexp-escape"},"506":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-11","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Duplicate named capturing groups § duplicate-names-must-be-in-different-alternatives"},"507":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-12","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"508":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-13","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Duplicate named capturing groups § backreferences"},"509":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-14","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"510":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-15","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Duplicate named capturing groups § can-you-refer-to-a-group-in-a-different-alternative"},"511":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-16","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"512":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-17","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2025: RegExp patterns"},"513":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-18","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2025-06-25, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"514":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-19","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"TC39 notes: duplicate named capture groups for Stage 4"},"515":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-20","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2024-04-08, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"516":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-21","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards"},"517":{"id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups-22","page_id":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/duplicate-named-capture-groups#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2025-06-26, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"518":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","type":"page","content":"Dynamic Code Brand Checks","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ESNext"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks"},"519":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-0","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#dynamic-code-brand-checks","content":"Dynamic Code Brand Checks"},"520":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-1","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"521":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-2","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"522":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-3","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"523":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-4","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#dynamic-code-brand-checks","content":"Host-defined code-like objects can carry trusted source into dynamic code evaluation."},"524":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-5","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#what-it-does","content":"`HostGetCodeForEval` lets a host extract source from an object that the host recognizes as code-like. The compilation guard receives the original arguments, the assembled source, and the compilation kind for `eval` and dynamic function constructors. Existing non-string values keep the early-return behavior unless a host recognizes them."},"525":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-6","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#gotchas","content":"ECMAScript does not provide a constructor for code-like objects; hosts define how such values are created and recognized. Code-like values are not proxyable under the proposed design."},"526":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-7","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 active proposals at the cutoff"},"527":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-8","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 stage record, published 2026-07-22, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"528":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-9","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"Dynamic Code Brand Checks § tldr"},"529":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-10","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"530":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-11","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"Dynamic Code Brand Checks § solution"},"531":{"id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks-12","page_id":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-code-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"532":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"page","content":"Dynamic import()","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2020"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import"},"533":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-0","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#dynamic-import","content":"Dynamic import()"},"534":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-1","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"535":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-2","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"536":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-3","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"537":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-4","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#support","content":"Support"},"538":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-5","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#related","content":"Related"},"539":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-6","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"540":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-7","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#dynamic-import","content":"`import(specifier)` evaluates a runtime expression as a module specifier and returns a promise for the resulting module namespace object."},"541":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-8","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#what-it-does","content":"`ImportCall` takes one `AssignmentExpression`, applies `ToString` to its value, and returns the promise of a capability created before the host is asked to load anything; a failing coercion rejects that promise instead of throwing. The host performs the load and reports the outcome by calling `FinishDynamicImport`, which resolves the promise with `GetModuleNamespace` of the requested record or rejects it with the failure. The host hook accepts a null referencing script or module, which is what allows the form outside any module. The proposal lists the differences from an `import` declaration: it is usable from a script, it is not hoisted, it accepts a computed string, and its presence creates no dependency that must be fetched before the containing module evaluates."},"542":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-9","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#gotchas","content":"A missing module produces a rejected promise, never a synchronous throw, so a bare `import(\"./absent.mjs\")` in an expression statement leaves an unhandled rejection. The argument is an expression rather than a specifier token: an object whose `toString` returns a path is accepted, because the call coerces the value before handing it to the host. Repeated calls for one specifier hand back the same namespace object and evaluate the module once, since the resolution step reads the already-evaluated record. The form is not a function value: it cannot be renamed, passed as a callback, or called with `Reflect.apply`, because it is a grammar production rather than a property of an object."},"543":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-10","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#support","content":"V8 shipped the form in 6.3, whose notes describe it as loading modules chosen by runtime conditions and mention lazy loading of code as the motivating case."},"544":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-11","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#related","content":"import-attributes"},"545":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-12","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#related","content":"source-phase-imports"},"546":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-13","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMAScript proposal: import() § example"},"547":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-14","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"548":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-15","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Import Calls"},"549":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-16","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"550":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-17","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: FinishDynamicImport"},"551":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-18","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"552":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-19","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: HostImportModuleDynamically"},"553":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-20","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"554":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-21","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Dynamic import() for stage 4"},"555":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-22","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2019-06-04, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"556":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-23","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"V8 release v6.3: JavaScript language features"},"557":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-24","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"Engine record, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"558":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-25","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 119th General Assembly"},"559":{"id":"/features/dynamic-import-26","page_id":"/features/dynamic-import","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/dynamic-import#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"560":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"page","content":"Ergonomic brand checks for private fields","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2022"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks"},"561":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-0","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#ergonomic-brand-checks-for-private-fields","content":"Ergonomic brand checks for private fields"},"562":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-1","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"563":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-2","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"564":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-3","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"565":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-4","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#related","content":"Related"},"566":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-5","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"567":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-6","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#ergonomic-brand-checks-for-private-fields","content":"The `in` operator takes a private name on its left side and answers whether the right operand carries that private element."},"568":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-7","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#what-it-does","content":"`RelationalExpression` gains the production `PrivateIdentifier in ShiftExpression`. Evaluating it resolves the identifier in the running private environment, requires the right operand to be an Object, and returns `true` when `PrivateElementFind` locates a matching entry. That lookup only inspects the object's own `[[PrivateElements]]` list. The check covers all three private kinds, and the champion presented it as reporting fields, private methods, and private accessors alike. The proposal's motivation is a check that neither throws nor discloses that a private field is the mechanism."},"569":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-8","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#gotchas","content":"The form is not total: the right operand must be an Object or the expression throws a `TypeError`, so `#amount in 5` throws where a `try`-based check would have returned `false`, and a guard against primitives still has to run first. A `Proxy` wrapping an instance reports `false`, because the lookup reads the `[[PrivateElements]]` of the object handed to it and a proxy has its own empty list; the same holds for `Object.create(Instance.prototype)`, which never ran instance initialization. The left operand is a literal private name, not a value: the proposal notes that this choice rules out any later shorthand where a bare `#x` would mean `this.#x`."},"570":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-9","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#related","content":"class-fields"},"571":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-10","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#related","content":"private-methods-and-accessors"},"572":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-11","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Ergonomic brand checks for Private Fields proposal § rationale"},"573":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-12","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"574":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-13","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Ergonomic brand checks for Private Fields proposal § in"},"575":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-14","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"576":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-15","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: Relational Operators grammar"},"577":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-16","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"578":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-17","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: Relational Operators evaluation"},"579":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-18","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"580":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-19","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2022: PrivateElementFind"},"581":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-20","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"582":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-21","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Ergonomic Brand Checks for Stage 4"},"583":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-22","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2021-07-14, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"584":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-23","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 123rd General Assembly"},"585":{"id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks-24","page_id":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ergonomic-brand-checks#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2022-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"586":{"id":"/features/error-cause","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"page","content":"Error cause","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2022"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause"},"587":{"id":"/features/error-cause-0","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#error-cause","content":"Error cause"},"588":{"id":"/features/error-cause-1","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"589":{"id":"/features/error-cause-2","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"590":{"id":"/features/error-cause-3","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"591":{"id":"/features/error-cause-4","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#support","content":"Support"},"592":{"id":"/features/error-cause-5","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#related","content":"Related"},"593":{"id":"/features/error-cause-6","page_id":"/features/error-cause","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/error-cause#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"594":{"id":"/features/error-cause-7","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#error-cause","content":"Error constructors take a trailing options object whose `cause` property is installed on the new error as a non-enumerable own property."},"595":{"id":"/features/error-cause-8","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#what-it-does","content":"`Error ( message [ , options ] )` calls `InstallErrorCause` after setting `message`. That operation checks `HasProperty(options, \"cause\")` and, when present, copies the value with `CreateNonEnumerableDataPropertyOrThrow`. The resulting property is writable and configurable but not enumerable. The same step appears in every `NativeError` constructor and in `AggregateError`, which runs it before collecting its `errors` list. The proposal's stated aim is a single spelling that tooling can rely on, replacing per-codebase conventions for attaching the original error. It also draws a line against `AggregateError`: `cause` accumulates depth along one failure path, while an aggregate collects unrelated errors caught in one place."},"596":{"id":"/features/error-cause-9","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#gotchas","content":"Presence, not value, decides installation: because the check is `HasProperty`, `new Error(\"m\", { cause: undefined })` has an own `cause`, while `new Error(\"m\", {})` and a plain `new Error(\"m\")` have none, so `Object.hasOwn(error, \"cause\")` is the only reliable test. A non-object second argument is silently dropped rather than rejected, since the same step requires `Type(options)` to be Object, so `new Error(\"m\", \"boom\")` installs nothing. The proposal notes that Firefox already accepted `fileName` and `lineNumber` as extra positional arguments and that an object with a `cause` property stays distinguishable from those strings."},"597":{"id":"/features/error-cause-10","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#support","content":"Node.js shipped the option in 16.9.0, whose notes show the `cause` option pointing at another error."},"598":{"id":"/features/error-cause-11","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#related","content":"aggregate-error"},"599":{"id":"/features/error-cause-12","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#sources","content":"Error Cause proposal § chaining-errors"},"600":{"id":"/features/error-cause-13","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"601":{"id":"/features/error-cause-14","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#sources","content":"Error Cause proposal § differences-with-aggregateerror"},"602":{"id":"/features/error-cause-15","page_id":"/features/error-cause","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/error-cause#