amic `import()` accepts an options object whose `with` property holds the attributes. The host validates supported keys and values before loading or executing the module."},"892":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-8","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#gotchas","content":"Attributes are part of a module request and can participate in cache identity according to host rules. Attribute values in the standardized grammar are strings, and unknown attributes can cause loading to fail."},"893":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-9","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#related","content":"json-modules"},"894":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-10","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#related","content":"dynamic-import"},"895":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-11","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Import Attributes proposal § proposed-syntax"},"896":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-12","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"897":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-13","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Import Attributes proposal § integration-of-modules-into-environments"},"898":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-14","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"899":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-15","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Import Attributes proposal § proposed-semantics-and-interoperability"},"900":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-16","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"901":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-17","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2025: Modules"},"902":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-18","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2025-06-25, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"903":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-19","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Import Attributes and JSON Modules for Stage 4"},"904":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-20","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2024-10-08, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"905":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-21","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards"},"906":{"id":"/features/import-attributes-22","page_id":"/features/import-attributes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-attributes#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2025-06-26, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"907":{"id":"/features/import-meta","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"page","content":"import.meta","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2020"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta"},"908":{"id":"/features/import-meta-0","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#importmeta","content":"import.meta"},"909":{"id":"/features/import-meta-1","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"910":{"id":"/features/import-meta-2","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"911":{"id":"/features/import-meta-3","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"912":{"id":"/features/import-meta-4","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#support","content":"Support"},"913":{"id":"/features/import-meta-5","page_id":"/features/import-meta","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"914":{"id":"/features/import-meta-6","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#importmeta","content":"`import.meta` gives each module one host-populated object for metadata such as its own location."},"915":{"id":"/features/import-meta-7","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#what-it-does","content":"Evaluating `import.meta` reads the active module's `[[ImportMeta]]` slot, and on first access creates an object with a null prototype, copies in the key-value records the host supplies, hands the object to the host's finalization hook, and stores it in the slot. That slot starts out empty on every Source Text Module Record and holds the object once ECMAScript code has read it. `HostGetImportMetaProperties` must return property keys with ECMAScript values, must complete normally, and defaults to an empty list, so a host that defines nothing yields a bare object. `HostFinalizeImportMeta` is the escape hatch for a host that needs to manipulate the object before code sees it, and it defaults to doing nothing. Using the form outside a module is an early error: it is a Syntax Error when the syntactic goal symbol is not `Module`. The proposal's stated aim is a general extensibility point so that each piece of host metadata does not need its own standardization, delivered lexically rather than through a temporarily set global."},"916":{"id":"/features/import-meta-8","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#gotchas","content":"The object has a null prototype, so `import.meta.hasOwnProperty` is not a function and `Object.prototype` helpers have to be called through `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call`. It is writable and shared for the life of the module record: the same object is returned on every access, which the proposal accepts on the grounds that the object is local to the module and can only be shared by passing it around, so one part of a module can see a property another part added. Which properties exist is a host decision, because the specification's own default is an empty list: code that reads `import.meta.url` depends on the host, not on the language. The form is refused at parse time in a script, so it cannot be used to detect whether code runs as a module."},"917":{"id":"/features/import-meta-9","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#support","content":"V8 shipped the meta-property in 6.4, whose notes record that the embedder supplies the host-specific metadata and that Chrome 64 exposed the module URL through `import.meta.url`."},"918":{"id":"/features/import-meta-10","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript proposal: import.meta § constraints"},"919":{"id":"/features/import-meta-11","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"920":{"id":"/features/import-meta-12","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript proposal: import.meta § will-this-object-be-locked-down-in-any-way"},"921":{"id":"/features/import-meta-13","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"922":{"id":"/features/import-meta-14","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Meta Properties"},"923":{"id":"/features/import-meta-15","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"924":{"id":"/features/import-meta-16","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Left-Hand-Side Expressions, Static Semantics: Early Errors"},"925":{"id":"/features/import-meta-17","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"926":{"id":"/features/import-meta-18","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: HostGetImportMetaProperties ( moduleRecord )"},"927":{"id":"/features/import-meta-19","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"928":{"id":"/features/import-meta-20","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: HostFinalizeImportMeta ( importMeta, moduleRecord )"},"929":{"id":"/features/import-meta-21","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"930":{"id":"/features/import-meta-22","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2020: Source Text Module Records"},"931":{"id":"/features/import-meta-23","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"932":{"id":"/features/import-meta-24","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"TC39 notes: import.meta for Stage 4, continued from the previous day"},"933":{"id":"/features/import-meta-25","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2020-04-01, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"934":{"id":"/features/import-meta-26","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"TC39 notes: import.meta for stage 4"},"935":{"id":"/features/import-meta-27","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2020-03-31, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"936":{"id":"/features/import-meta-28","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"V8 release v6.4: ECMAScript language features"},"937":{"id":"/features/import-meta-29","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Engine record, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"938":{"id":"/features/import-meta-30","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 119th General Assembly"},"939":{"id":"/features/import-meta-31","page_id":"/features/import-meta","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-meta#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2020-06-16, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"940":{"id":"/features/import-text","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"page","content":"Import Text","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ESNext"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text"},"941":{"id":"/features/import-text-0","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text#import-text","content":"Import Text"},"942":{"id":"/features/import-text-1","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"943":{"id":"/features/import-text-2","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"944":{"id":"/features/import-text-3","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"945":{"id":"/features/import-text-4","page_id":"/features/import-text","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"946":{"id":"/features/import-text-5","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#import-text","content":"The `text` import attribute loads a referenced resource as a string."},"947":{"id":"/features/import-text-6","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#what-it-does","content":"`import text from \"./message.txt\" with { type: \"text\" }` binds the decoded contents as the default import. The proposal does not add an encoding option. A caller that needs a specific encoding instead imports bytes and decodes them explicitly."},"948":{"id":"/features/import-text-7","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#gotchas","content":"Text import depends on the host's module loading support and is not equivalent to fetching a resource at runtime. A non-default text encoding requires the separate byte-import path described by the proposal."},"949":{"id":"/features/import-text-8","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"TC39 active proposals at the cutoff"},"950":{"id":"/features/import-text-9","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"TC39 stage record, published 2026-07-22, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"951":{"id":"/features/import-text-10","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"Import Text § outline-of-a-proposed-solution"},"952":{"id":"/features/import-text-11","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"953":{"id":"/features/import-text-12","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"Import Text § shortcomings"},"954":{"id":"/features/import-text-13","page_id":"/features/import-text","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/import-text#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"955":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"page","content":"Iterator chunking","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ESNext"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking"},"956":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-0","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking#iterator-chunking","content":"Iterator chunking"},"957":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-1","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"958":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-2","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"959":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-3","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"960":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-4","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/iterator-chunking#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"961":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-5","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#iterator-chunking","content":"Iterator methods produce non-overlapping chunks or overlapping sliding windows as arrays."},"962":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-6","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#what-it-does","content":"`Iterator.prototype.chunks(size)` lazily consumes up to `size` values for each result array and retains a shorter last chunk. `Iterator.prototype.windows(size)` advances by one value and emits full overlapping windows by default. Its second argument accepts `\"allow-partial\"` to emit a shorter terminal window."},"963":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-7","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#gotchas","content":"Sizes must be integral numbers in the inclusive range from one through `2**32 - 1`. An invalid size closes the underlying iterator before throwing."},"964":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-8","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#sources","content":"TC39 active proposals at the cutoff"},"965":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-9","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#sources","content":"TC39 stage record, published 2026-07-22, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"966":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-10","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-chunking#sources","content":"Iterator Chunking § motivation"},"967":{"id":"/features/iterator-chunking-11","page_id":"/features/iterator-chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url"