ple iterable inputs in sequence."},"978":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-7","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#what-it-does","content":"The method validates that each argument is iterable when called, then opens and consumes each iterator only when iteration reaches it. Arrays or other one-element iterables can place immediate values between longer sequences."},"979":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-8","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#gotchas","content":"Arguments must be iterable objects; bare primitive values are not single-item inputs. Closing the concatenated iterator closes the currently active inner iterator according to the sequencing algorithm."},"980":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-9","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#related","content":"iterator-helpers"},"981":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-10","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#sources","content":"Iterator Sequencing § chosen-solution"},"982":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-11","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"983":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-12","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2026: Iterator.concat"},"984":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-13","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2026-06-30, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"985":{"id":"/features/iterator-concat-14","page_id":"/features/iterator-concat","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-concat#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Iterator Sequencing for Stage 4"},"986":{"id"