irectly to iterator objects."},"996":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-6","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#what-it-does","content":"`map`, `filter`, `take`, `drop`, and `flatMap` return lazy iterator helpers. `reduce`, `toArray`, `forEach`, `some`, `every`, and `find` consume the iterator, while `Iterator.from` wraps iterator-like inputs."},"997":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-7","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#gotchas","content":"Transformation helpers are single-use and lazy because they wrap an underlying iterator rather than producing an array. Iterator closing propagates through helper chains when consumption stops early."},"998":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-8","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"Iterator Helpers proposal § added-methods"},"999":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-9","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"1000":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-10","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"Iterator Helpers proposal § iterator-helpers-and-the-generator-protocol"},"1001":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-11","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"1002":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-12","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2025: Iterator objects"},"1003":{"id":"/features/iterator-helpers-13","page_id":"/features/iterator-helpers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/iterator-helpers#sources","content":"ECMA-262 spec