d-2","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"1558":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-3","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"1559":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-4","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"1560":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-5","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#await-dictionary","content":"`Promise.allKeyed` and `Promise.allSettledKeyed` preserve dictionary keys while combining promise results."},"1561":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-6","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#what-it-does","content":"`Promise.allKeyed` waits for the values of an object's own enumerable properties and fulfills with an object using the same keys. `Promise.allSettledKeyed` produces keyed fulfillment or rejection records. Enumerable symbol keys participate alongside string keys."},"1562":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-7","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#gotchas","content":"Only own enumerable properties are included; inherited and non-enumerable properties are omitted. Getters run while the input entries are collected, and an abrupt getter completion rejects the result."},"1563":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-8","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"TC39 active proposals at the cutoff"},"1564":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-9","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"TC39 stage record, published 2026-07-22, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"1565":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-10","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"Await dictionary of Promises § proposed-solution"},"1566":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-11","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"1567":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-12","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"Await dictionary of Promises § additional-api"},"1568":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-13","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"1569":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-14","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"Await dictionary of Promises draft specification"},"1570":{"id":"/features/promise-all-keyed-15","page_id":"/features/promise-all-keyed","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-keyed#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-25"},"1571":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"page","content":"Promise.allSettled","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2020"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled"},"1572":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-0","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#promiseallsettled","content":"Promise.allSettled"},"1573":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-1","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"1574":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-2","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"1575":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-3","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"1576":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-4","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#support","content":"Support"},"1577":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-5","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#related","content":"Related"},"1578":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-6","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/promise-all-settled#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"1579":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-7","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#promiseallsettled","content":"`Promise.allSettled` waits for every input promise to settle and fulfils with one outcome record per input."},"1580":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-8","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#what-it-does","content":"`Promise.allSettled` creates a promise capability from its receiver, iterates the argument, and closes the iterator when the collection step fails. The collection step reads `resolve` from the constructor once, throws a `TypeError` when it is not callable, appends `undefined` to the result list for each input, and attaches a resolve and a reject element function for that index; the outer promise resolves only when the shared remaining count reaches zero. A fulfilled input stores an object with `status` set to `\"fulfilled\"` and a `value` property, and a rejected input stores `status` set to `\"rejected\"` with a `reason` property, each written at its own index. The proposal's stated distinction from the other combinators is that this one never short-circuits and always waits for all of its input values."},"1581":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-9","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#gotchas","content":"The returned promise has no rejection path of its own, so a `.catch` attached to it never runs for an input failure and an unread `status` field silently hides one. Each record carries one payload key: a fulfilled entry has no `reason` and a rejected entry has no `value`, so reading `results[i].value` on a failure yields `undefined` rather than an error. Positions come from the input index, not the settle order, so the slowest input keeps its place in the array. An empty iterable fulfils with an empty array, because the remaining count starts at one and is decremented as soon as iteration ends. A thenable that calls both of its callbacks is recorded once: that same step creates one `alreadyCalled` record and installs it on the resolve and the reject element function of the index, so `{ then(resolve, reject) { reject(error); resolve(value); } }` produces a single `\"rejected\"` entry."},"1582":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-10","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#support","content":"V8 shipped the method in 7.6, whose notes present it as a signal that every input promise has settled."},"1583":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-11","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#related","content":"promise-any"},"1584":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-12","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/promise-all-settled#sources","content":"ECMAScript proposal: Promise.allSettled § overview-and-motivation"},"1585":{"id":"/features/promise-all-settled-13","page_id":"/features/promise-all-settled