ts#what-it-does","content":"The defaults are `strict: true`, `module: \"esnext\"`, the latest supported annual ECMAScript target, `noUncheckedSideEffectImports: true`, and `libReplacement: false`. An explicit configuration value still overrides each default."},"2551":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-9","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#migration","content":"Set the previous value explicitly for any changed default that the project cannot adopt in the same upgrade. Prefer an explicit runtime target rather than depending on the floating target when output compatibility is fixed."},"2552":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-10","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#compatibility","content":"Projects with complete explicit configurations are unaffected by these defaults. Sparse configurations can receive new type errors, different module emit, newer JavaScript output, side-effect import errors, or disabled replacement-library lookup."},"2553":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-11","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#related","content":"ts-lib-replacement"},"2554":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-12","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 6.0"},"2555":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-13","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2026-03-23, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"2556":{"id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults-14","page_id":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-compiler-defaults#sources","content":"TypeScript 6.0 release notes: Simple Default Changes"},"2557":{"id":"/features/ts-compi