g","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"2639":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-3","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"2640":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-4","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#constant-indexed-access-narrowing","content":"Control-flow checks narrow `object[key]` when both the object and key remain constant."},"2641":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-5","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#what-it-does","content":"After a guard such as `typeof object[key] === \"string\"`, later access through the same object and key receives the narrowed type. Reassigning either operand prevents this analysis."},"2642":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-6","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.5"},"2643":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-7","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-06-20, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2644":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-8","page_id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.5 release notes: indexed access narrowing"},"2645":{"id":"/features/ts-constant-indexed-access-narrowing-9","page_id":"/