d numeric special-value names are rejected."},"2737":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-6","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#what-it-does","content":"Structurally matching enums no longer remain compatible when corresponding known member values differ. Known string members do not match members assumed to be numeric. Member names `Infinity`, `-Infinity`, and `NaN` are invalid numeric names."},"2738":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-7","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#migration","content":"Align values across declarations that are meant to interoperate, or stop assigning between distinct enums. Rename disallowed members to ordinary identifiers. The new diagnostics identify the differing member or invalid name."},"2739":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-8","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.4"},"2740":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-9","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2741":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-10","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 release notes: enum assignability"},"2742":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-11","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2743":{"id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions-12","page_id":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-enum-restrictions#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 release notes: enum member names"},"2744":