x-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#erasablesyntaxonly","content":"`erasableSyntaxOnly` reports TypeScript constructs that require JavaScript generation rather than type erasure."},"2754":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-6","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#what-it-does","content":"The check rejects enums, parameter properties, runtime namespaces, `import =`, and `export =`. It accepts type annotations and other syntax that a stripping runtime can remove while leaving valid JavaScript."},"2755":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-7","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#gotchas","content":"This option checks erasability, not the target runtime's module rules. The release notes recommend combining it with `verbatimModuleSyntax` so import elision does not conceal incompatible module syntax."},"2756":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-8","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.8"},"2757":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-9","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2025-02-28, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2758":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-10","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.8 release notes: erasableSyntaxOnly"},"2759":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-11","page_id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2760":{"id":"/features/ts-erasable-syntax-only-12","page_id":"/