ecks-6","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#what-it-does","content":"For a conditional expression directly inside `return`, each branch is compared with the declared return type. A branch typed `any` no longer absorbs an incompatible sibling branch into an `any` union before that comparison."},"2904":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-7","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#gotchas","content":"The special handling applies to conditional expressions directly returned from functions with declared return types. It does not remove the general assignability behavior of `any` elsewhere."},"2905":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-8","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.8"},"2906":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-9","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2025-02-28, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2907":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-10","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.8 release notes: Granular Checks for Branches in Return Expressions"},"2908":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-11","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"2909":{"id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks-12","page_id":"/features/ts-granular-return-branch-checks","tags":[],"type":"te