nd cannot be disabled."},"3175":{"id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering-8","page_id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering#what-it-does","content":"Union, property, display, and declaration ordering follows the deterministic algorithm previewed by `stableTypeOrdering`. The compiler also adopts the preceding release's strict, module, target, side-effect import, library replacement, root-directory, and ambient-type defaults. An inferred union reaches declaration output in one order no matter where its members were first encountered. The preceding release's notes state that the native compiler always prints the content-ordered union."},"3176":{"id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering-9","page_id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering#migration","content":"Run the prior compiler with `stableTypeOrdering` enabled and remove any assumption that the native compiler can return to allocation-based ordering. Add explicit types where order-dependent inference changes a result."},"3177":{"id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering-10","page_id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering#compatibility","content":"Projects that compile under the preceding release with stable ordering and without suppressed deprecations are the documented compatibility baseline."},"3178":{"id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering-11","page_id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering#related","content":"ts-stable-type-ordering"},"3179":{"id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering-12","page_id":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mandatory-stable-type-ordering#sources","content":"Announci