ading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3205":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-2","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3206":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-3","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#migration","content":"Migration"},"3207":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-4","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#compatibility","content":"Compatibility"},"3208":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-5","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3209":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-6","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","content":"Mapped types preserve known tuple elements when an `any` rest element is present."},"3210":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-7","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#what-it-does","content":"Applying a mapped type to a variadic tuple no longer decomposes it into manufactured singleton tuples. Property keys follow the tuple positions, so `Keys<[string, string, ...T, string]>` yields `[\"0\", \"1\", ...Keys<T>, number]` where it previously repeated `\"0\"`. Required elements after a rest element instantiate correctly."},"3211":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-8","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#migration","content":"Update code that read the repeated key type or relied on the collapsed result, and expect an excessive-instantiation-depth error where a earlier fix leaked a type parameter."},"3212":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-9","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#compatibility","content":"Operations such as `Promise.all` can infer a specific head element and an `any[]` tail where the full result previously collapsed to `any`. Type assertions that relied on the collapsed type can change behavior."},"3213":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-10","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.4"},"3214":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-11","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3215":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-12","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","content":"TypeScript pull request 57031: preserve mapped tuple elements"},"3216":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-13","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","content":"Pull request, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3217":{"id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation-14","page_id":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-mapped-tuple-rest-preservation#sources","conte