declarations, declaration maps, and selected strictness options. It keeps a grouped handful of commented options and a link to the TSConfig reference in place of the full option catalogue. The earlier output turned on six settings and left every other option commented out beside its description. The 5.8 baseline sets `target: \"es2016\"`, `module: \"commonjs\"`, `esModuleInterop`, `forceConsistentCasingInFileNames`, `strict`, and `skipLibCheck`."},"3227":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-7","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#gotchas","content":"These settings affect newly generated files only. Existing `tsconfig.json` files are not rewritten by an upgrade. The documented mechanism is the output of an explicit `tsc --init` invocation."},"3228":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-8","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.9 § minimal-and-updated-tsc---init"},"3229":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-9","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2025-08-01, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3230":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-10","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.9 release notes: Minimal and Updated tsc --init"},"3231":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-11","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3232":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-12","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-minimal-init#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.8 default tsc --init output baseline"},"3233":{"id":"/features/ts-minimal-init-13","page_id":"/features/ts-minimal-init","tags":[],"type":"t