,"page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3533":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-6","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#nullish-return-implicit-any-checks","content":"Some contextually generic callbacks returning `null` or `undefined` now report implicit `any`."},"3534":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-7","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#what-it-does","content":"A function expression contextually typed by a signature that returns a generic type, and lacking a return-type annotation, reports TS7011 for an implicit `any` return. `p.catch(() => null)` on a `Promise<number>` is the published example."},"3535":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-8","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#migration","content":"Annotate the callback's return type, or enable `strictNullChecks`, which keeps the contextual return type usable."},"3536":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-9","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#compatibility","content":"The diagnostic appears only with `noImplicitAny` enabled and `strictNullChecks` disabled, so a project already using null-aware checking sees no change."},"3537":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-10","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.7"},"3538":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-11","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-11-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3539":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-12","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.7 release notes: nullish return implicit any"},"3540":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-13","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3541":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-14","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.7 stable release"},"3542":{"id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any-15","page_id":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-nullish-return-implicit-any#sources","content":"Release tag, published 2024-11-22, reviewed 2026-07-24"},"3543":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","type":"page","content":"Parallel build controls","breadcrumbs":["typescript","TS 7.0"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls"},"3544":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-0","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#parallel-build-controls","content":"Parallel build controls"},"3545":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-1","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3546":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-2","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"3547":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-3","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3548":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-4","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#parallel-build-controls","content":"The native compiler parallelizes parsing, type checking, emit, and project-reference builds with configurable worker counts."},"3549":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-5","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#what-it-does","content":"`--checkers` controls type-checker workers, while `--builders` controls concurrent project-reference builders under build mode. `--singleThreaded` constrains checking, parsing, and emit to one thread. Type-checker work is divided deterministically for a fixed worker count."},"3550":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-6","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#gotchas","content":"Checker and builder counts multiply during project-reference builds, so their combined concurrency can exceed available resources. Varying checker count can expose order-dependent results; a fixed count keeps environments aligned."},"3551":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-7","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 § custom-scaling-parallelization-and-controls"},"3552":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-8","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2026-07-08, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3553":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-9","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 7.0 § project-reference-builder-parallelization"},"3554":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-10","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2026-07-08, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3555":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-11","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"typescript/v7.0.2 stable release"},"3556":{"id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls-12","page_id":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-parallel-build-controls#sources","content":"Release tag, published 2026-07-08, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3557":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","type":"page","content":"Preserved narrowing after last assignments","breadcrumbs":["typescript","TS 5.4"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing"},"3558":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-0","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#preserved-narrowing-after-last-assignments","content":"Preserved narrowing after last assignments"},"3559":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-1","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3560":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-2","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3561":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-3","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3562":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-4","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#preserved-narrowing-after-last-assignments","content":"Narrowed parameters and local variables retain their types inside later non-hoisted closures."},"3563":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-5","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#what-it-does","content":"The checker finds the last assignment to a parameter or `let` variable and preserves a preceding narrowing in closures created after that point. An assignment from any nested function prevents the preservation because that write can occur later."},"3564":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-6","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.4"},"3565":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-7","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3566":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-8","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 release notes: preserved closure narrowing"},"3567":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-9","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3568":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-10","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 stable release"},"3569":{"id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing-11","page_id":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-preserved-closure-narrowing#sources","content":"Release tag, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3570":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"page","content":"Primitive intersection reduction","breadcrumbs":["typescript","TS 5.4"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction"},"3571":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-0","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#primitive-intersection-reduction","content":"Primitive intersection reduction"},"3572":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-1","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3573":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-2","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3574":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-3","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#compatibility","content":"Compatibility"},"3575":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-4","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3576":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-5","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#primitive-intersection-reduction","content":"Intersections between type variables and primitive types reduce according to their constraint overlap."},"3577":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-6","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#what-it-does","content":"A fully overlapping primitive intersection can reduce to the type variable, while a disjoint intersection reduces to `never`. Partial overlap retains only viable constituents."},"3578":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-7","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#compatibility","content":"Inferred and displayed intersection types can become narrower, affecting overloads and assignments that depended on the earlier unreduced form."},"3579":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-8","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.4"},"3580":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-9","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3581":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-10","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 release notes: primitive intersection reduction"},"3582":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-11","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"TypeScript release notes, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3583":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-12","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"TypeScript 5.4 stable release"},"3584":{"id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction-13","page_id":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-primitive-intersection-reduction#sources","content":"Release tag, published 2024-03-06, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3585":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"page","content":"Reference directive declaration emit","breadcrumbs":["typescript","TS 5.5"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit"},"3586":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-0","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#reference-directive-declaration-emit","content":"Reference directive declaration emit"},"3587":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-1","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3588":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-2","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3589":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-3","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#migration","content":"Migration"},"3590":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-4","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3591":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-5","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#reference-directive-declaration-emit","content":"Declaration emit stops synthesizing reference directives and preserves authored directives only when marked."},"3592":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-6","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#what-it-does","content":"A source directive with `preserve=\"true\"` remains in emitted declarations. Other authored directives are omitted, and the compiler no longer creates directives based on inferred ambient dependencies."},"3593":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-7","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#migration","content":"Mark directives that downstream consumers require with `preserve=\"true\"` and ensure package or configuration types include dependencies that were previously synthesized. The release notes state that older compilers ignore the unknown preservation attribute."},"3594":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-8","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#sources","content":"Announcing TypeScript 5.5"},"3595":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-9","page_id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit#sources","content":"TypeScript release announcement, published 2024-06-20, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3596":{"id":"/features/ts-reference-directive-emit-10","page_id":"