base64-hex#gotchas","content":"Hex decoding accepts upper- or lowercase digits but emits lowercase text. Base64 decoding accepts ASCII whitespace; strict final-chunk handling also rejects nonzero overflow bits."},"3875":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-8","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Uint8Array to/from base64 and hex § basic-api"},"3876":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-9","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3877":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-10","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Uint8Array to/from base64 and hex § base64-options"},"3878":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-11","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3879":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-12","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Uint8Array to/from base64 and hex § faq"},"3880":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-13","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3881":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-14","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2026: Uint8Array objects"},"3882":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-15","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2026-06-30, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3883":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-16","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"TC39 notes: Uint8Array base64 and hex for Stage 4"},"3884":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-17","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2025-07-28, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3885":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-18","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards"},"3886":{"id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex-19","page_id":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/uint8array-base64-hex#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2026-07-01, reviewed 2026-07-23"},"3887":{"id":"/features/weakref","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"page","content":"WeakRef","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2021"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref"},"3888":{"id":"/features/weakref-0","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#weakref","content":"WeakRef"},"3889":{"id":"/features/weakref-1","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3890":{"id":"/features/weakref-2","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3891":{"id":"/features/weakref-3","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"3892":{"id":"/features/weakref-4","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#support","content":"Support"},"3893":{"id":"/features/weakref-5","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#related","content":"Related"},"3894":{"id":"/features/weakref-6","page_id":"/features/weakref","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3895":{"id":"/features/weakref-7","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#weakref","content":"A `WeakRef` holds an object without keeping it alive, and `deref` returns either that object or `undefined` once it has been collected."},"3896":{"id":"/features/weakref-8","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#what-it-does","content":"`new WeakRef(target)` requires `new`, rejects a non-object target, records it in `[[WeakRefTarget]]`, and passes it to `AddToKeptObjects`. `deref` reads that slot and returns the target, or `undefined` when the reference has been cleared. The kept-alive list is what makes repeated reads consistent: `ClearKeptObjects` empties it, and implementations are expected to run it when a synchronous sequence of execution completes, so either every `deref` in one such run returns the object or all of them return `undefined`. The proposal's motivating structure is a cache keyed by name whose values may be dropped, which `WeakMap` cannot express because it is weak over keys rather than values."},"3897":{"id":"/features/weakref-9","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#gotchas","content":"A `deref` call keeps the object alive for the rest of the synchronous run, so a script that reads the reference and then forces collection still sees the object: `WeakRefDeref` calls `AddToKeptObjects` before returning the target, and that list is only emptied between runs. Clearing is never something to schedule around, because the specification promises no collection at all and therefore describes this behavior with \"may\"; the proposal lists generational collection, incremental collection, and engine-held references among the reasons one object outlives another. The reference itself is not the leak that matters: the entry holding it stays in the surrounding `Map` after the target is gone, which is the residue the companion registry removes. The constructor is strict about both requirements, so `WeakRef({})` without `new` and `new WeakRef(\"id\")` each throw a `TypeError`."},"3898":{"id":"/features/weakref-10","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#support","content":"V8 shipped weak references in 8.4, whose example notes that a freshly created reference is guaranteed to survive the first turn of the event loop."},"3899":{"id":"/features/weakref-11","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#related","content":"finalization-registry"},"3900":{"id":"/features/weakref-12","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#related","content":"symbols-as-weakmap-keys"},"3901":{"id":"/features/weakref-13","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"WeakRefs TC39 proposal § weak-references"},"3902":{"id":"/features/weakref-14","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3903":{"id":"/features/weakref-15","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"WeakRefs TC39 proposal § a-note-of-caution"},"3904":{"id":"/features/weakref-16","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3905":{"id":"/features/weakref-17","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"ECMAScript 2021: WeakRef ( target )"},"3906":{"id":"/features/weakref-18","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"ECMA-262 specification, published 2021-06-22,