tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"TC39 notes: WeakRefs for Stage 4 / CleanupSome for Stage 2/3"},"3918":{"id":"/features/weakref-30","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"Committee notes, published 2020-07-21, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3919":{"id":"/features/weakref-31","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"V8 release v8.4: Weak references and finalizers"},"3920":{"id":"/features/weakref-32","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"Engine record, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3921":{"id":"/features/weakref-33","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"Ecma International approves new standards at the 121st General Assembly"},"3922":{"id":"/features/weakref-34","page_id":"/features/weakref","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/weakref#sources","content":"Ecma General Assembly record, published 2021-06-22, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3923":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"page","content":"Well-formed JSON.stringify","breadcrumbs":["ecmascript","ES2019"],"tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify"},"3924":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-0","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#well-formed-jsonstringify","content":"Well-formed JSON.stringify"},"3925":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-1","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#what-it-does","content":"What it does"},"3926":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-2","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#before--after","content":"Before / after"},"3927":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-3","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#gotchas","content":"Gotchas"},"3928":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-4","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#support","content":"Support"},"3929":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-5","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#related","content":"Related"},"3930":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-6","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#sources","content":"Primary sources"},"3931":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-7","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#well-formed-jsonstringify","content":"`JSON.stringify` emits a `\\uXXXX` escape for every unpaired surrogate code unit instead of copying it into the result."},"3932":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-8","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#what-it-does","content":"`QuoteJSONString` walks the value as UTF-16 encoded code points and now escapes a code point with `UnicodeEscape` when it has the same numeric value as a leading or a trailing surrogate, alongside the existing rule for code points below U+0020. A well-formed surrogate pair decodes to a supplementary code point, so it takes the final branch and is copied through unchanged. The proposal states the problem this removes: the result claimed to be UTF-16 while an isolated code unit in D800–DFFF is ill-formed, which left no UTF-8 representation for the returned text."},"3933":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-9","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#gotchas","content":"The escape appears in the serialized text only; the string being serialized still holds the lone surrogate, so a length or index check on the value is unaffected. `JSON.parse` turns the six-character escape back into the same code unit, so the round trip is lossless and a consumer that already accepted the ill-formed output sees an equivalent value. Paired surrogates are still emitted as the raw supplementary character rather than as two escapes, so only ill-formed input changes shape. The escape is a reverse solidus, `u`, and the code unit's value as a four-digit lowercase hexadecimal number padded with zeroes, which matters to code that compares serialized text byte for byte."},"3934":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-10","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#support","content":"V8 escaped lone surrogates from 7.2, whose before-and-after pair shows `JSON.stringify('\\uD800')` moving from a replacement character to `'\"\\\\ud800\"'`."},"3935":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-11","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#related","content":"well-formed-unicode-strings"},"3936":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-12","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#sources","content":"ECMAScript proposal: Well-formed JSON.stringify § motivation"},"3937":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-13","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify#sources","content":"TC39 proposal repository, reviewed 2026-07-26"},"3938":{"id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify-14","page_id":"/features/well-formed-json-stringify","tags"