by receiver, since the typed-array closure compares numerically instead of using the string comparison of `Array.prototype.toSorted`: `[10, 9, 1].toSorted()` yields `[1, 10, 9]` while `new Uint8Array([10, 9, 1]).toSorted()` yields `[1, 9, 10]`. `Array.prototype.toSorted` also rejects a non-callable comparator with a `TypeError` before touching the receiver."],[2335,"139"],[2338,"144"],[1229,"2026-07-24"],[1232,"2026-07-24"],[1235,"2026-07-24"],[1238,"2026-07-24"],[1241,"2026-07-24"],[2336,"2026-07-24"],[2339,"2026-07-24"],[2342,"2026-07-24"],[637,"2026-07-26"],[640,"2026-07-26"],[2083,"2026-07-26"],[2086,"2026-07-26"],[1237,"22.18.0, default"],[1228,"22.6.0, flagged and experimental"],[1231,"22.7.0, transform flag and experimental"],[1234,"23.6.0, default and experimental"],[636,"24.0.0"],[2082,"24.0.0"],[1240,"24.12.0, stable"],[639,"24.3.0"],[2085,"24.5.0"],[2341,"26.0.0"],[1478,"A `catch` clause may drop both its parameter and the surrounding parentheses when the handler never reads the thrown value."],[3897,"A `deref` call keeps the object alive for the rest of the synchronous run, so a script that reads the reference and then forces collection still sees the object: `WeakRefDeref` calls `AddToKeptObjects` before returning the target, and that list is only emptied between runs. Clearing is never something to schedule around, because the specification promises no collection at all and therefore describes this behavior with \"may\"; the proposal lists generational collection, incremental collection, and engine-held references among the reasons one object outlives another. The reference itself is not the leak that matters: the entry holding it stays in the surrounding `Map` after the target is gone, which is the residue the companion registry removes. The constructor is strict about both requirements, so `WeakRef({})` without `new` and `new WeakRef(\"id\")` each throw a `TypeError`."],[738,"A `FinalizationRegistry` calls one callback with a registered held value after the garbage collector reclaims the object it was registered against."],[1090,"A `JSON.parse` reviver receives a third context argument whose `source` property contains the original token text for an unmodified primitive. `JSON.rawJSON` creates a frozen placeholder for validated primitive JSON text, `JSON.isRawJSON` detects it, and `JSON.stringify` emits its text without quoting it."],[1533,"A `MethodDefinition` names its member with a `ClassElementName`, which may be a `PrivateIdentifier`. When that name is a Private Name, method evaluation returns a PrivateElement whose `[[Kind]]` is `method` for a plain definition and `accessor` for a `get` or `set` definition, instead of defining a property. Those PrivateElements are copied onto every new instance before its field initializers run. Adding a private method to an object that already carries the same private name throws a `TypeError`. The three class-features proposals were requested in one agenda item, and the sub-proposal's own repository now records only that it merged into class fields."],[2380,"A `ModuleItem` parses its `StatementListItem` with the `Await` parameter set, so an `await` expression is legal directly in a module body. Module evaluation marks such a record with `[[HasTLA]]`, sets `[[AsyncEvaluation]]`, and counts each asynchronous dependency in `[[PendingAsyncDependencies]]` so that a module with pending dependencies is not executed yet. Executing one of these modules creates a promise capability and resumes the graph from its fulfilment or rejection handler. `[[Status]]` gains the value `evaluating-async` for a module that has executed and is awaiting top-level completion. The proposal's own framing is that a module behaves like one large async function whose importers wait before evaluating their bodies."],[458,"A `static { … }` member runs statements once during class definition, with the constructor as `this` and access to the class's private names."],[2458,"A `Uint8Array` is not assignable 