id not participate has no pair: an unmatched group's slot is `undefined` rather than an empty range, so `/a+(?<Z>z)?/d.exec(\"xaaay\").indices[1]` is `undefined` and the matching `indices.groups.Z` is too. The `groups` property always exists on the array even when the pattern declares no names, in which case its value is `undefined`, so `Object.hasOwn(match.indices, \"groups\")` is `true` while `match.indices.groups` reads as nothing. Without the flag there is no `indices` property at all, because the result-building step is guarded by `hasIndices`; the search cost of collecting offsets is only paid when the flag opts in."],[1870,"A capture group written `(?<name>…)` is readable through `match.groups.name`, `\\k<name>`, and `$<name>`."],[427,"A class body accepts a `FieldDefinition`, which is a `ClassElementName` with an optional initializer, and a `ClassElementName` may be a `PrivateIdentifier` written with a leading `#`. A public field is installed with `CreateDataPropertyOrThrow`, and a declaration with no initializer installs the value `undefined`. A private field is appended to the instance's `[[PrivateElements]]` list instead of becoming a property, and a second attempt to add the same private name to one object throws a `TypeError`. Reading a private name from an object that carries no matching entry also throws a `TypeError`. Field declarations, private methods, and static class features were requested in one agenda item, and the committee advanced all three in a single decision. The proposal's stated aim is that declared state is visible in the class definition and present on every instance."],[426,"A class body declares instance state directly, and a leading `#` restricts a declared name to code written inside that body."],[3577,"A fully overlapping primitive intersection can reduce to the type variable, while a disjoint intersection reduces to `never`. Partial overlap retains only viable constituents."],[3534,"A function expression contextually typed by a