4 and hex § faq"],[3057,"Under `isolatedModules`, an imported type cannot share a name with a local value unless the import is explicitly type-only."],[3503,"Under `module: \"nodenext\"`, the compiler stops reporting an error solely because a CommonJS file requires an ECMAScript module. The mode models the runtime restriction that the target graph cannot contain top-level `await`. The release notes tie the check to Node's synchronous require behavior."],[1921,"Unicode property escapes: High-level API"],[1919,"Unicode property escapes: Motivation"],[1925,"Unicode property escapes: Unicode-aware version of \\d"],[1923,"Unicode property escapes: What about backwards compatibility?"],[1946,"Unicode sets mode supports nested character classes, intersection with `&&`, subtraction with `--`, string literals through `\\q{}`, and Unicode properties of strings. It incorporates Unicode mode while defining revised case-insensitive complement behavior."],[3175,"Union, property, display, and declaration ordering follows the deterministic algorithm previewed by `stableTypeOrdering`. The compiler also adopts the preceding release's strict, module, target, side-effect import, library replacement, root-directory, and ambient-type defaults. An inferred union reaches declaration output in one order no matter where its members were first encountered. The preceding release's notes state that the native compiler always prints the content-ordered union."],[2276,"Unique symbols are accepted wherever a weak collection previously demanded an object, so a key needs no object to stand in for it."],[2549,"Unspecified compiler options now select strict checking, ECMAScript modules, a floating annual target, checked side-effect imports, and disabled library replacement."],[2875,"Update buffer-dependent annotations and compatible `@types/node` versions when assignments involving `Buffer`, typed arrays, or `ArrayBuffer` begin to fail."],[3211,"Update code that read the repeated key type or relied on the collapsed result, and expect an excessive-instantiation-depth error where a earlier fix leaked a type parameter."],[1222,"Use `erasableSyntaxOnly` and `verbatimModuleSyntax` during type checking, and write type-only imports with the `type` keyword. A project needing transforms, configuration-driven paths, or full syntax requires a separate TypeScript execution path."],[3059,"Use `import type`, add an inline `type` modifier, or rename one binding. These forms give single-file compilers enough information to erase the import safely."],[2459,"Use a typed array with an explicit buffer parameter when the backing store is known, or pass the typed array's `buffer` property to an API that requires the buffer itself. Node projects should also use declarations that account for the generic typed-array base."],[3157,"Use an editor integration that speaks to the native LSP server. Keep the compatibility language service for projects that require plugins, template-aware embedding, or a programmatic compiler object."],[3358,"Use NodeNext for code executed directly by Node or bundler resolution for a compatible downstream resolver. Remove `baseUrl` and place its prefix in each `paths` target, or add an explicit catch-all mapping when lookup-root behavior is intentional."],[3280,"Use the extension and package type that match runtime format, and replace unsafe default imports from ECMAScript dependencies."],[3121,"Using `module` to declare a named internal namespace is an error."],[139,"V8 4.7 lists the method under upcoming ES features and describes it as returning a boolean for membership, while the proposal was still at Stage 3."],[706,"V8 5.2 announces the operator as replacing `Math.pow`, and its example uses both the infix form and `**=`."],[1481,"V8 accepted the clause without a parameter in 6.6, whose example handles an exception with no binding in scope."],[1343,"V8 added the built-in in 7.3, whose example feeds it the array returned by `Object.entries` to recover an eq